I need to estimate populations from aerial photos. The detection probability decreases with distance from the center of the photo, so distance sampling seems to be a good fit for the problem. But from what I can gather, the Distance and  mrds  packages require either circular (point) or transect samples. Is there way to fit distance detection models to square regions using these packages? I could do it by cutting off the corners to make it round, but that throws out nearly 1/4 of the area...and an important 1/4 as well.

-Dan

